  "description": "Calvin University's Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry is accredited by the American Chemical Society (ACS), and therefore students have the opportunity to earn degrees that are directly accredited by the ACS. To meet the requirements for an accredited ACS degree, students take additional chemistry courses to round out their chemical and biochemical studies in preparation for graduate school. The accredited ACS major also increases the emphasis on research, requiring all students to have and present on a research experience as part of their graduation requirements.",
